{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLQva1uCvPYfnTuUe2gD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the bug: `sympy.zeros(4,2).is_upper` now returns `True` instead of raising `IndexError`.\n\n**Cause:** in a tall matrix (more rows than columns), the loop asked for column numbers up to `i - 1` even when the matrix doesn't have that many columns. In `sympy/matrices/matrices.py`, it now stops at the last real column.\n\nThe fix is two lines in that file:\n- `is_upper` (line 1115): `range(i)` → `range(min(i, self.cols))`\n- `_eval_is_upper_hessenberg` (line 644): this had the same bug, so `is_upper_hessenberg` also crashed on tall matrices. `range(i - 1)` → `range(min(self.cols, i - 1))`\n\n**Checks:**\n- `zeros(4,2).is_upper` gives `True`.\n- `zeros(5,2).is_upper_hessenberg` gives `True`.\n- A 4x2 matrix with a nonzero entry below the diagonal correctly gives `False` for `is_upper`.\n- I ran `test_matrices.py` and `test_commonmatrix.py`: 199 passed and 5 failed. The same 5 fail without my change, so they were already broken and aren't caused by this fix. They include `test_eigen_vects` and `test_from_ndarray`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":512,"cache_read_input_tokens":20657,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":512},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5e259d5-3e1f-49cc-81c2-b660b136e7d2","uuid":"cd9cec09-caf0-45c6-83fb-2bf0ef195425","timestamp":"2026-11-23T19:29:28.741Z","request_id":"req_011ChLQvZKj6NPC28V3gWX96"}
